ricana cortada por negarse a cantar ante público segregado, icono gay sin poder decirlo y etiquetada de «bachelor girl». «I Just Don’t Know What to Do with Myself» fue su primera obra maestra. «You Don’t Have to Say You Love Me» (marzo de 1966), adaptación de un tema de San Remo de Pino Donaggio con letra de Wickham y Simon Napier-Bell, cantada en la escalera del estudio de Philips, fue número 1 a finales de abril y la consagró como diva trágica.","color":"#38bdf8","family":"Pop de estudio: Spector, Beach Boys, Meek","link":"https://volteret4.github.io/1966/#dusty-springfield"}],"book_tracks":[{"id":74251731323600,"artist":"Gene Pitney","artist_id":115471535978731,"title":"24 Hours from Tulsa","year":1963,"ess":0,"yt":"zugy2rkSM7g","kind":null,"book":{"id":1,"title":"1966: The Year the Decade Exploded","author":"Jon Savage","url":"https://volteret4.github.io/1966/"},"scene":"Dusty Springfield","scene_id":22485426612515,"scene_link":"https://volteret4.github.io/1966/#dusty-springfield","chapters":["Mayo: Walkin’ My Cat Named Dog: la mística de la feminidad y la independencia femenina"],"pages":[[1,131]]}],"mentions":[{"book":"1966: The Year the Decade Exploded","author":"Jon Savage","page":112,"text":"…charts on both sides of the Atlantic, Tanega found that she was part of the music industry. She was quickly added to a six-week package tour with Gene Pitney, the McCoys, Len Barry and others. ‘Oh, that was an eye-opener. It was such an education to learn about pop. How can you be prepared for what goes…"},{"book":"1966: The Year the Decade Exploded","author":"Jon Savage","page":131,"text":"…the editor of Ready Steady Go!, so Dusty was regularly featured on the programme, acting as commère, swapping barbs with the Beatles, miming with Gene Pitney to a sped-up version of ‘24 Hours from Tulsa’ and singing ‘I Only Want to Be with You’, as well as her cover of Arthur Alexander’s ‘Every Day I Have…"}],"podcast":[],"awards":[],"concerts":[],"xref":[],"charts":[{"id":57377377